      "text": "Temple Hills got its name from Edward Temple, who lived beside Henson Creek in a home called Moor Park in the 1860s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Temple_Hills%2C_Maryland"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The community borders Hillcrest Heights, Marlow Heights, Camp Springs and Oxon Hill, keeping it tightly knit with neighboring areas.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Temple_Hills%2C_Maryland"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Most of the neighborhood’s homes were built between the 1950s and 1970s, giving the area a mid‑century feel.",
